        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0288" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.3212/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-24T16:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. Brazilian Government having asked the Carranza Government to accept Feitosa,
                    Brazilian Minister to Paraguay, as Brazilian Minister to Mexico and the Carranza
                    Government having fallen before giving an answer, the present Mexican Government
                    agreed to accept Feitosa although since it did so the Brazilian Government has
                    not again referred to the matter. Present Mexican Government then named Alvaro
                    Torre Díaz, Mexican Minister to Brazil and started him toward Rio de Janeiro on
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Avare</hi> which is due here to-morrow.</p>
                <p>Brazilian Ministry of Foreign Affairs which wishes to cooperate with present
                    Washington policy in regard to recognition of present Mexican Government is
                    embarrassed by Díaz’ prospective arrival, <pb facs="0289" n="189" xml:id="pg189"
                    /> more especially because before leaving for Europe Rodrigo Octavio, Under
                    Secretary of State, stated to Mexican Chargé d’Affaires that Brazil would
                    consult the American Government in regard to Díaz reception.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
